WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.534 --> 00:00:15.534
"Who are you?" Gliss' mother screamed at Morb.

2
00:00:15.535 --> 00:00:17.777
"How did you get past our Shield?"

3
00:00:17.778 --> 00:00:22.172
"It's him!" Zann shouted. "The man we were telling you about!"

4
00:00:22.173 --> 00:00:27.808
Morb ignored him. "Freeze," he intoned, pointing at Gliss' parents.

5
00:00:27.809 --> 00:00:33.093
Instantly her parents froze in place. Her mother's eyes were wide and frightened.

6
00:00:33.094 --> 00:00:36.114
Her father's mouth was open in the middle of a shout.

7
00:00:36.115 --> 00:00:39.537
"Mom! Dad!" Gliss shrieked.

8
00:00:39.538 --> 00:00:45.667
Morb made a beckoning motion. A second later two large, hideous trolls appeared!

9
00:00:45.668 --> 00:00:49.817
"Take them to the dungeon," Morb ordered the trolls.

10
00:00:49.818 --> 00:00:54.934
Another quick flash and the trolls disappeared—along with Gliss' parents.

11
00:00:54.935 --> 00:00:57.570
"No!" Gliss screamed.

12
00:00:57.571 --> 00:01:02.644
"We have to get out of here!" Zann shouted. He rubbed his hands together.

13
00:01:02.645 --> 00:01:07.470
Perda was already doing the same. But not Gliss. She just stood there.

14
00:01:07.471 --> 00:01:11.466
"She's in shock," Zann said. "Even if we get away . . ."

15
00:01:11.467 --> 00:01:15.346
There was no time to say more. Morb had turned toward them.

16
00:01:15.347 --> 00:01:20.890
He glanced at Perda with disinterest. But when he saw Gliss, he smirked.

17
00:01:20.891 --> 00:01:24.294
"Another Red," he said, raising his hand.

18
00:01:24.295 --> 00:01:31.574
"No!" Darb cried. He reached into his pocket and flung a handful of panic bugs into Morb's face.

19
00:01:31.575 --> 00:01:38.227
"Ugh!" Morb exclaimed as the little insects panicked, releasing their foul-smelling odor.

20
00:01:38.228 --> 00:01:41.273
"Get away from me, you repulsive creatures!"

21
00:01:41.274 --> 00:01:47.158
It only took Morb a few seconds to blast the bugs to smithereens. But that was enough time.

22
00:01:47.159 --> 00:01:50.187
"Get her!" Zann shouted at Perda.

23
00:01:50.188 --> 00:01:53.888
Perda grabbed Gliss. Zap! They both disappeared.

24
00:01:53.889 --> 00:02:00.167
Zann dived for Darb. His hand closed on his friend's arm just as Morb spun toward them.

25
00:02:00.168 --> 00:02:05.105
The man's eyes narrowed. "Don't you dare!" he exclaimed.

26
00:02:05.106 --> 00:02:07.286
"This time you're not getting away from—"

27
00:02:07.287 --> 00:02:09.015
Zap!

28
00:02:09.016 --> 00:02:11.145
Splash!

29
00:02:11.146 --> 00:02:15.909
"Drat!" Zann cried. "How come I always land in the swamp?"

30
00:02:15.910 --> 00:02:20.267
"Forget that," Darb said breathlessly. "At least you got us out of there!"

31
00:02:20.268 --> 00:02:26.394
Zann nodded. "Good thinking using those panic bugs. You probably saved us all."

32
00:02:26.395 --> 00:02:31.155
"Thanks." Darb looked sad. "I wish he hadn't blasted them though."

33
00:02:31.156 --> 00:02:35.053
Zann wasn't going to waste time mourning a bunch of smelly insects.

34
00:02:35.054 --> 00:02:40.139
"We'd better find the girls." He waved a hand to summon a spy fly.

35
00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:46.418
Suddenly Morb materialized in front of them. "Stop right there!" he exclaimed.

36
00:02:46.419 --> 00:02:49.947
"What?" Zann cried, startled. "How did you—"

37
00:02:49.948 --> 00:02:54.173
He didn't bother to finish. Grabbing Darb, he zapped them away again.

38
00:02:54.174 --> 00:02:57.903
This time he aimed for the cave where Zing was waiting.

39
00:02:57.904 --> 00:03:03.557
"Whew!" he said when they landed. "That was close. How in the world did he—"

40
00:03:03.558 --> 00:03:09.531
Again Morb appeared. "Give up, Red! You can't escape!"

41
00:03:09.532 --> 00:03:12.834
Zann instantly grabbed both Darb and Zing.

42
00:03:12.835 --> 00:03:17.221
This time he didn't have time to think of a destination.

43
00:03:17.222 --> 00:03:21.306
"Ouch!" Darb exclaimed as they landed on a craggy boulder.

44
00:03:21.307 --> 00:03:28.458
"How's Morb doing this?" Zann cried. "He can't follow us through a Zap unless we leave him a trail!"

45
00:03:28.459 --> 00:03:33.885
Darb didn't answer. He just grabbed Zann as Morb appeared again.

46
00:03:33.886 --> 00:03:42.619
Morb cackled. "I told you, it's no use trying to escape. My magic is far superior to—"

47
00:03:42.620 --> 00:03:45.899
Zap!

48
00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:53.495
Darb yanked on Zann's arm as they landed near a stream where they'd often fished for moon minnows. "Come with me," he urged.

49
00:03:53.496 --> 00:03:57.175
"What?" Zann was rubbing his hands, preparing to zap again.

50
00:03:57.176 --> 00:04:01.915
He hoped his magical energy held out until he could figure out what to do.

51
00:04:01.916 --> 00:04:06.454
"Come on!" Darb took off running, with Zing flying behind him.

52
00:04:06.455 --> 00:04:09.839
"Darb! Wait!" Zann chased after them.

53
00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:12.890
"You'll never escape that guy without magic!"

54
00:04:12.891 --> 00:04:17.010
Darb didn't answer. He dove into a thick clump of bushes.

55
00:04:17.011 --> 00:04:21.035
Zann followed. "What are you doing?"

56
00:04:21.036 --> 00:04:26.654
"Hush!" Darb crawled forward, peering out from among the dense branches.

57
00:04:26.655 --> 00:04:30.444
Morb soon appeared in the spot where the boys had landed.

58
00:04:30.445 --> 00:04:34.823
"This game is becoming tiresome." He glanced around.

59
00:04:34.824 --> 00:04:41.302
"You might as well give up. Trust me, you do not want to anger me further."

60
00:04:41.303 --> 00:04:45.319
"Quick, let's zap away again before he—" Zann hissed.

61
00:04:45.320 --> 00:04:51.315
"No!" Darb cut him off. "Don't you get it? He's tracking your magic somehow."

62
00:04:51.316 --> 00:04:56.716
Could Darb be right? Zann had never heard of someone tracking people through their magic.

63
00:04:56.717 --> 00:05:01.415
Then he remembered. "I think we studied that last year," he said.

64
00:05:01.416 --> 00:05:05.440
"But that kind of magic has been banned since the Old Times."

65
00:05:05.441 --> 00:05:11.583
"Flash Freezes are illegal too," Darb reminded him. "And Morb has been using them."

66
00:05:11.584 --> 00:05:15.026
"So what can we do?" Zann felt helpless.

67
00:05:15.027 --> 00:05:19.883
If Morb could find him every time he used magic, there was no escape.

68
00:05:19.884 --> 00:05:22.438
"Let's get to the Hollow," Darb said.

69
00:05:22.439 --> 00:05:25.995
"His magic can't find us there. It'll give us time to think."

70
00:05:25.996 --> 00:05:30.313
Zann gulped. The Hollow? He would feel even more helpless there!

71
00:05:30.314 --> 00:05:36.276
But Darb was right. They had to get away from Morb long enough to figure out what was going on.

72
00:05:36.277 --> 00:05:39.810
"Okay." Zann sneaked another peek at Morb.

73
00:05:39.811 --> 00:05:44.560
"But first I've got to use magic once more to let Perda know what's happening."

74
00:05:44.561 --> 00:05:49.409
Darb looked worried. "Morb will know where you are as soon as you summon the moth.

75
00:05:49.410 --> 00:05:52.078
You won't have time to inscribe the message."

76
00:05:52.079 --> 00:05:54.685
Zann bit his lip. "Good point."

77
00:05:54.686 --> 00:06:00.997
Darb smiled. "Then again I just happen to know that message moths like to rest in shady underbrush.

78
00:06:00.998 --> 00:06:04.608
So if we can find one without using magic . . ."

79
00:06:04.609 --> 00:06:09.828
He carefully crawled around, peering under leaves.

80
00:06:09.829 --> 00:06:14.099
Seconds later he cupped his hands around a fluttering insect.

81
00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:24.392
"Awesome!" Zann whispered. Grabbing the moth, he quickly inscribed his message onto its wings: Don't use ANY magic! Meet at the Hollow.

82
00:06:24.393 --> 00:06:29.706
Darb was peering out. "He's getting closer," he whispered. "Better do it now."

83
00:06:29.707 --> 00:06:36.651
"Perda," Zann told the moth. He rubbed his fingers together and released the creature.

84
00:06:36.652 --> 00:06:41.360
"Aha!" Morb howled triumphantly from very close by.

85
00:06:41.361 --> 00:06:50.306
"Zap!" Zann yelled, focusing on the spot right outside the Hollow.
